(p/'README.md').write_text('''# Oreone International website starter\n\nA responsive, multi-page static website starter for Oreone International Limited.\n\n## Pages\n- Home (`index.html`)\n- About (`about.html`)\n- What We Do (`what-we-do.html`)\n- Who We Serve (`who-we-serve.html`)\n- Partnerships (`partnerships.html`)\n- Insights (`insights.html`)\n- Contact (`contact.html`)\n- Privacy notice (`privacy.html`)\n\n## Preview locally\nOpen `index.html` in a browser, or run a local server from this folder (for example `python -m http.server 8000`) and visit `http://localhost:8000`.\n\n## Before production launch\n1. Replace `https://oreone.com/` canonical URLs with the real live domain if different.\n2. Replace the CSS-generated text mark with the official Oreone logo asset when supplied in a usable file format.\n3. Review all copy and confirm the address, telephone and email.\n4. Connect a real form service or backend. The current contact form opens a pre-filled email draft and does not transmit/store submissions automatically.\n5. Replace placeholder Insights topics with researched, edited articles before indexing article URLs.\n6. Review privacy notice, consent needs, analytics and security for the actual deployment.\n7. Optimise final image assets and verify all pages, metadata and mobile behaviour.\n\n## Technical notes\n- Semantic HTML and responsive CSS\n- Per-page title and meta description\n- Organization JSON-LD starter markup\n- `robots.txt` and `sitemap.xml` starter files\n- Accessible navigation toggle and basic contact form validation\n\nExternal background imagery currently uses Unsplash image URLs. For production, download/licence and optimise selected images, and add the official brand assets.\n''')
